The Concept: Grouping back-to-back days of system successes or failures into clean "start" and "end" date streaks.
Skills Used: The "Gaps and Islands" Pattern, Window Functions (ROW_NUMBER()), Date Subtraction.

Solved the classic "Gaps and Islands" SQL architecture problem to track continuous streaks of data over time.
Used the ROW_NUMBER() window function combined with date subtraction to automatically generate a unique ID for back-to-back consecutive days.
Condensed a disorganized daily log of system statuses into a clean report showing the start dates, end dates, and total duration of each streak.
